.TH ACMERS 1 "2026-10-23" "acmers 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acmers \- zero-dependency ACME client for SSL/TLS certificate automation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acmers
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBacmers\fR is a minimal-dependency Rust CLI for automatic SSL/TLS
certificate issuance and renewal via the ACME protocol (RFC 8555).
It supports DNS-01 challenge validation for 200+ DNS providers,
ported from the acme.sh project.
.PP
Single binary, zero runtime dependencies beyond glibc.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBregister\fR \-\-email \fIaddr\fR [\-\-ca \fIname\fR] [\-\-server \fIurl\fR] [\-\-test] [\-\-eab\-kid \fIid\fR \-\-eab\-hmac\-key \fIkey\fR]
Register an ACME account. Use \fB--ca\fR to select a CA preset and
\fB--test\fR for Let's Encrypt staging. Accounts are stored per ACME server.
EAB credentials are only needed for the first registration at a CA that
requires them.
.TP
\fBissue\fR \-d \fIdomain\fR... \-\-dns \fIprovider\fR \-\-email \fIaddr\fR [options]
Issue a certificate for one or more domains using the DNS-01 challenge.
The \fB--dns\fR flag selects the DNS provider (see \fBlist-providers\fR).
Use \fB--ca\fR for a CA preset, \fB--test\fR for staging, and \fB--server\fR for
a non-default directory URL.
.TP
\fBrenew\fR [\-d \fIdomain\fR] [\-\-all] [\-\-force] [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-days \fIn\fR]
Renew one certificate, or every stored certificate when no domain is given.
Renewal preserves all subject alternative names and wildcards.
.TP
\fBrevoke\fR \-d \fIdomain\fR [\-\-reason \fIreason\fR] [\-\-delete-after-revoke]
Revoke a certificate. Reasons: unspecified, keycompromise,
affiliationchanged, superseded, cessationofoperation, privilegewithdrawn.
.TP
\fBlist\-providers\fR
List all available DNS providers with their required environment variables.
.TP
\fBcron\fR
Alias for \fBrenew --all\fR, intended for cron and systemd timers.
.TP
\fBcertificates\fR
List stored certificates with their domains and remaining validity.
.TP
\fBshow\fR \-d \fIdomain\fR
Show the stored configuration and expiry for a certificate.
.TP
\fBshow\-account\fR [\-\-server \fIurl\fR] [\-\-test]
Show the active ACME account.
.TP
\fBdelete\fR \-d \fIdomain\fR
Delete a stored certificate and its configuration.
.SH ISSUE AND RENEW OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-path\fR, \fB\-\-key\-path\fR, \fB\-\-fullchain\-path\fR, \fB\-\-chain\-path\fR \fIfile\fR
Copy the corresponding artifact to a service path after issuance.
.TP
\fB\-\-reloadcmd\fR \fIcommand\fR
Run a command after installing certificates on an actual renewal.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\-hook\fR, \fB\-\-pre\-hook\fR, \fB\-\-post\-hook\fR \fIcommand\fR
Run commands around issuance. Deploy hooks run only when a certificate is
issued or renewed. Hooks receive \fBRENEWED_LINEAGE\fR and
\fBRENEWED_DOMAINS\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-servers\fR \fIip[,ip...]\fR, \fB\-\-dns\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
Poll DNS resolvers until the challenge TXT record is visible, instead of
waiting a fixed delay. Default resolvers come from \fI/etc/resolv.conf\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-preferred\-chain\fR \fIissuer\fR
Select a matching alternate certificate chain when the CA offers one.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Load provider credentials from a file containing \fIKEY=VALUE\fR lines. Blank
lines and lines beginning with \fB#\fR are ignored, and surrounding quotes are
removed. Values from \fB-e\fR override the file, which overrides the process
environment. For example:
.PP
.nf
  CF_Token=your-cloudflare-api-token
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-dnssleep\fR \fIseconds\fR
Fixed wait before challenge validation, used as a fallback when propagation
polling is unavailable.
.SH CA SELECTION AND EAB
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\fR \fIname\fR
Select a built-in CA preset: \fBletsencrypt\fR, \fBletsencrypt\-staging\fR,
\fBzerossl\fR, \fBgoogle\fR, \fBsslcom\fR, \fBsslcom\-rsa\fR, \fBbuypass\fR,
\fBbuypass\-test\fR, or \fBsectigo\fR. The default is Let's Encrypt production.
\fB--server\fR overrides the preset directory URL while keeping the preset's EAB
requirement, and a known CA directory passed via \fB--server\fR infers the EAB
requirement. \fB--test\fR selects Let's Encrypt staging and conflicts with a
non-Let's Encrypt preset.
.TP
\fB\-\-eab\-kid\fR \fIid\fR, \fB\-\-eab\-hmac\-key\fR \fIkey\fR
External Account Binding credentials for account registration. ZeroSSL, Google
Trust Services, SSL.com, and Sectigo require EAB; Let's Encrypt and Buypass do
not. The values may instead come from \fBACME_EAB_KID\fR and
\fBACME_EAB_HMAC_KEY\fR. EAB is only needed when an account is first created:
renewals with an existing account do not need it, and the secrets are never
stored on disk.
.PP
Buypass discontinued TLS/SSL certificate issuance in October 2025. Its presets
remain for existing accounts and test endpoints but cannot issue new
certificates; Buypass also issued RSA-only certificates, which acmers does not
support yet.
.PP
.nf
  acmers register --email you@example.com --ca zerossl \\
    --eab-kid kid-from-ca --eab-hmac-key hmac-key-from-ca
.fi
.SH DNS PROVIDERS
acmers supports 200+ DNS providers. Each provider requires specific
environment variables for authentication. Run \fBacmers list-providers\fR
to see the full list and required variables.
.PP
Common providers and their environment variables:
.TP
\fBcloudflare\fR
\fBCF_Token\fR or \fBCF_Key\fR + \fBCF_Email\fR
.TP
\fBdigitalocean\fR
\fBDO_API_KEY\fR
.TP
\fBroute53\fR
\fBAWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\fR + \fBAWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\fR
.TP
\fBduckdns\fR
\fBDuckDNS_Token\fR
.TP
\fBhe\fR (Hurricane Electric)
\fBHE_Username\fR + \fBHE_Password\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.acmers/
Per-user configuration and certificate state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/acmers/
System-wide certificate state used when running as root, including the packaged
systemd service.
.TP
.I /etc/acmers/env
Provider credentials for unattended renewal. Keep this file mode 0600. The
packaged service loads it automatically, and the cron fallback passes it with
\fB--env-file\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/acmers.timer
Twice-daily renewal timer, enabled on package installation. The packaged
timer uses a 12-hour randomized delay and \fBPersistent=true\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All DNS provider credentials are passed via environment variables, or loaded from
\fI/etc/acmers/env\fR by the packaged service and with \fB--env-file\fR.
\fBACME_EAB_KID\fR and \fBACME_EAB_HMAC_KEY\fR provide External Account Binding
credentials when \fB--eab\-kid\fR and \fB--eab\-hmac\-key\fR are not given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Error occurred (configuration, provider, or ACME protocol error).
